{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you","id":99767,"title":"What does being a Solar mean to You?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-26T22:27:59-07:00","id":99767,"title":"What does being a Solar mean to You?","content":"The title says it all. I am curious what being a Solar means to you guys. Here's my view:<br /> <br /> Perhaps there is nothing you can do. Perhaps the end is inevitable.<br /> <br /> The Realm which made Creation stable is threatening to tear itself apart. Forces of the Underworld seek to cast Creation into Oblivion. The Yozis send their champions and demons to wreak vengeance upon a world that has forgotten them. The various nations once under the thumb of the Realm seek independence, but perhaps will turn upon each other in order to make their nation the dominant one. The Scavenger Lands are too weak and divided to resist the forces of the Realm and the Underworld.<br /> Forget calling on heaven for help for it is too corrupted to care. Forget calling upon the Unconquered Sun, your god, for help as he has turned his back on Creation. Forget uniting the other Exalts under your banner; they hate each other and you too much, even as the forces that threaten Creation grow stronger by the hour.<br /> What about you? You have the power of the sun but everyone views you as a demon. The Immaculate Order declares you to be Anathema, a powerful being that threatens Creation, the Realm, and the Dragonblooded. As you learn more about the past of your past incarnation, you find that there is some truth to their statements. You find that your predecessors were once heroes who defeated the Yozis long ago but they became cruel and decadent towards the end of the First Age. Their deaths meant that Creation would survive but in a lesser form. This means that the glories of the First Age can never return. You are hunted, cursed by others, and hated, and you may too become just as cruel and just as decadent as your predecessors.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there is nothing you can do. Perhaps it is better to wait for the end of the world.<br /> <br /> \u2026No, you will do no such thing.<br /> <br /> Perhaps preventing the end is impossible, but then again defeating the Yozis and banishing them to Malfeas was though impossible, but your predecessors managed to achieve that. The power that lies in you allows you to accomplish the impossible.<br /> You are Kingmaker as by your might and will you can create a powerful nation from the Scavenger Realms or any other nation under the purview of the Realm. This nation will be powerful enough to replace the Realm. Or you can save the Realm, but you remold it in your image and you can lead it to even greater glory.<br /> You are World-shaker as by your might and will you can destroy the forces of the Underworld and prevent Creation from falling into Oblivion. You are able to challenge and defeat the Champions of the Yozis and remind them of who defeated them in the first place.<br /> You are Miracle-weaver, as you purge the Heavens of its corruption and restore its duty of overlooking Creation. You can make the Unconquered Sun turn his face back toward and restore his faith in his chosen. You can make the other Exalts put aside their differences and remind them that their power is meant to serve Creation. You do not seek to restore the glories of the First Age; instead you build new wonders unseen before. You can even stave off the insanity that once claimed your predecessors, allowing you to lead Creation into a new Golden Age. By doing this you are adored, blessed, and loved by the people of Creation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you can do something. Perhaps you can save Creation.<br /> <br /> This is what being a Solar means to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r312/WuseMajor/t4q8xrt1_zps39b23a54.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/251-seifus","name":"Seifus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar251_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T23:38:14-07:00","id":99790,"title":"","content":"You are hopeless.<br /> <br /> Your power is overwhelming, strong enough to destroy anything that might stand against you and overcome any task placed in front of you. But your unseen, unknown curse will ruin you who have never known failure, just as it ruined your previous incarnations. You may undo the taint of Oblivion, you may restore the ramparts against the encroach of the Wyld, and you may even reunite the Exalted host and create an age of glory to surpass any wonders of the lost First Age. And then history will simply repeat itself as you go mad without ever realizing anything is wrong.<br /> <br /> Look to the powers of the Underworld, Malfeas and Autochthon for salvation. The ones who have known despair, known failure, and known service rather than rulership are capable of doing that which you are not, and keeping their minds whole. Perhaps one of them will save you from yourself, if you do not destroy or enslave them all first in the pursuit of your glory built on sand. Otherwise shine, arrogant sun, so sure you can save the world, until your heart turns to iron and you burn out.<br /> <br /> Solars are my least favorite Exalts. And that's a shame, because I wanted to like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T23:47:08-07:00","id":99792,"title":"","content":"It's like being a fantasy <a href=\"http://youtu.be/5G8f4m2y9_k\" target=\"_blank\">Commander Shepard</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T23:49:31-07:00","id":99793,"title":"","content":"It means having the power to shape the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T23:55:43-07:00","id":99795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Couch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99790#post99790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are hopeless.<br /> <br /> Your power is overwhelming, strong enough to destroy anything that might stand against you and overcome any task placed in front of you. But your unseen, unknown curse will ruin you who have never known failure, just as it ruined your previous incarnations. You may undo the taint of Oblivion, you may restore the ramparts against the encroach of the Wyld, and you may even reunite the Exalted host and create an age of glory to surpass any wonders of the lost First Age. And then history will simply repeat itself as you go mad without ever realizing anything is wrong.<br /> <br /> Look to the powers of the Underworld, Malfeas and Autochthon for salvation. The ones who have known despair, known failure, and known service rather than rulership are capable of doing that which you are not, and keeping their minds whole. Perhaps one of them will save you from yourself, if you do not destroy or enslave them all first in the pursuit of your glory built on sand. Otherwise shine, arrogant sun, so sure you can save the world, until your heart turns to iron and you burn out.<br /> <br /> Solars are my least favorite Exalts. And that's a shame, because I wanted to like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or until you ask yourself &quot;Why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; And then go on to fix the Great Cures. I've done it like... three times in my games.<br /> <br /> More seriously: To me, being a Solar is about looking at the world, seeing it's shitty condition and saying &quot;Someone has to fix this mess, and since everyone has had ten thousand years to do it and blew it, I'll have to do it myself.&quot; How you fix the mess, who you ally with, who you screw over, how both of those come back to bite you and how you deal with that is where the real fun is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:46:24-07:00","id":99813,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ygI-2F8ApUM&amp;t=2m07s\" target=\"_blank\">Being a Solar is rather like being Adrien Brody.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 03-27-2014, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T00:57:11-07:00","id":99817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99795#post99795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or until you ask yourself &quot;Why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; And then go on to fix the Great Cures. I've done it like... three times in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be more appreciative of this if it did not require being more perceptive than every character in the First Age combined and make the Usurpation a case of literally nobody paying attention. It contributes nothing to the motif of actions having consequences and in fact actively detracts from it by providing an excuse for bad decisions. I'd much rather just remove it and make the fall of the Solars their own individual faults, with each new Solar free to decide for themselves how they're going to act when given phenomenal cosmic power without restrictions on living space.<br /> <br /> That said, what you describe is what I wish Solars were like for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T01:00:06-07:00","id":99820,"title":"","content":"I'm personally a staunch believer in that exaltations are very impartial when it comes selecting hosts<br /> <br /> They only choose potential - and that doesn't have to be potential for good. The cruelest dictator, the most scrupulous murderer. And not necesarily under the best circumstances.<br /> <br /> The best of intentions can equally be corrupted by both loyalty and hate - say a slave in Nexus exalts with the wish to end slavery, a noble purpose indeed - and then he vows to burn the city to the ground because he sees it as one of the biggest 'engines' in the slavery 'machine'<br /> <br /> Or if a Linowan exalts as a solar with dreams of producing the finest timber products in creation - and decides to chop down all the trees of Halta because fuck Halta that's why.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being a solar simply means that you have the potential for such greatness within a given field that you have been blessed by heaven with powers unchecked and unchained by any authority. It's no guarantee that you'll be nice about it, and its no guarantee that you won't become a posterboy for bronze faction propaganda when they say &quot;We need to kill all solars - again&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T01:23:23-07:00","id":99831,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't describe being a Solar with any connections to the present geopolitical state of Creation. Being a Solar is about eternal ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1661-zeroregistry","name":"ZeroRegistry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T02:06:59-07:00","id":99845,"title":"","content":"You're a regular guy (or girl). But someone with potential, with skills. But you live in a world of wonders, of magical creatures, gods and demons.<br /> But you've got dreams. You want to be something more, someone more.<br /> And then one day, you are. You suddenly go from being a normal person to someone with incredible power. Your dreams are in your grasp. But... most people now think you're a demon, a monster. The rest worship you. Strange memories fill your head, and everyone who tells you what is going on has an agenda.<br /> You've been suddenly transformed from a human to a god. How will you deal with it? Will you use your powers for good, or evil?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T02:29:08-07:00","id":99849,"title":"","content":"I haven't played Solars, but my experience with them is more or less this. <br /> <br /> You are unbreakable. You never give up. When the entire world stands against you, you will be the one to tell it to stand aside and move, and crush it into submission if it doesn't. You will see your ideals come to pass or die in the attempt. No compromise, no relenting - there have been enough compromises in the world, and look where it ended. You are now one of the greatest, and you will reclaim your birthright. <br /> <br /> (And in case the wording didn't make it clear, <i>none of this is a good thing</i>)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T02:36:33-07:00","id":99852,"title":"","content":"Hope, your in a world where the average mortal seems to get squashed by anything and everything. The world is beseiged by demons and the undead and murder fairies. The heavens are corrupt and the little traitors that took your crown and your one thousand year old paramore is stuck between killing you and marrying you shot gun style. So in this world, you seem to be the only hope for everything continuing on in any reasonable way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T02:36:54-07:00","id":99853,"title":"","content":"Being a Solar is about having the potential to accomplish anything and the will to pull it off regardless of the obstacles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2551-lucil","name":"Lucil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T03:02:23-07:00","id":99866,"title":"","content":"Solars are, metaphorically speaking, the exalts who can toss a coin and calmly tell you that it will land heads. Not because they can control the coin in midair or see its future, but from sheer will and ability to make it happen.<br /> <br /> They are the splat who look at what anyone else would consider a huge risk, accept the responsibility, and get on with making it pay off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1414-pyrosorc","name":"Pyrosorc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T03:28:29-07:00","id":99881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99792#post99792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like being a fantasy <a href=\"http://youtu.be/5G8f4m2y9_k\" target=\"_blank\">Commander Shepard</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious Sword/Shotgun Princess!<br /> <br /> Being a Solar means you can always win, if you put your mind to it. There is no thing 'impossible' for you, and there is no obstacle too great. You WILL win. Not because it's your destiny. Destiny means something else decided your path for you. You're a Solar Exalted, and you will win because it's your right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T04:17:56-07:00","id":99912,"title":"","content":"I set myself to do what I do because that is my will, and no one else can do it. The world treats me as a god and as a monster. If these are true, I will live the part. If these are false, I will prove them wrong. Either way I will not be denied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T04:56:31-07:00","id":99924,"title":"","content":"Being a Solar is being number one,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Uiyaqnj2FZ4\" data-code=\"Uiyaqnj2FZ4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Uiyaqnj2FZ4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> the one with the touch,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A52--FKUQgU\" data-code=\"A52--FKUQgU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/A52--FKUQgU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> a Prince of the Universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VEJ8lpCQbyw\" data-code=\"VEJ8lpCQbyw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VEJ8lpCQbyw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's knowing that whatever you want, nothing's gonna stand in your way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=73dc1D8YHBg\" data-code=\"73dc1D8YHBg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/73dc1D8YHBg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:04:29-07:00","id":99926,"title":"","content":"<i>Just remember what old Jack Burton does when the earth quakes, the poison arrows fall from the sky, and the pillars of Heaven shake. Yeah, Jack Burton just looks that big old storm right in the eye and says &quot;Give me your best shot. I can take it.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/73-ares","name":"Ares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar73_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:10:07-07:00","id":99928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99795#post99795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or until you ask yourself &quot;Why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; And then go on to fix the Great Cures. I've done it like... three times in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of a digression, but I sort of feel like if your game's treatment of a curse-curing plot begins with the PCs asking themselves &quot;why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; then it's indicative of a situation where the players don't really buy into the curse as a game concept but the ST didn't want to remove or retool it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:15:53-07:00","id":99931,"title":"","content":"I see the Solars as a fiery beacon of unrestrained idealism put into action, flickering brightly, so brightly, that they cannot contain it. That idealism may lead them to good or evil, or anything in between, but nobody is left the same for their passing, and nobody can forget them once they are gone [pedant comment here. PS: you suck]. They live on eternally in the people they effect, like all people who are larger than life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 03-27-2014, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T05:50:18-07:00","id":99944,"title":"","content":"I mostly see being a Solar as being able to be awesome in whichever way you really want. There are definite themes and trappings inherent to Solar-ness, but I don't find them nearly as &quot;mandatory &quot; as the other splats'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":46,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","user":"Oramus","date":". 03-27-2014, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T06:05:56-07:00","id":99956,"title":"","content":"What rises must fall. What has fallen may rise again, or fall further still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:27:35-07:00","id":99995,"title":"","content":"&quot;Someone should do something about this.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I could do something about this.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I will do something about this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2160-elemental","name":"Elemental","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"412"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:41:18-07:00","id":100005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99928#post99928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bit of a digression, but I sort of feel like if your game's treatment of a curse-curing plot begins with the PCs asking themselves &quot;why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; then it's indicative of a situation where the players don't really buy into the curse as a game concept but the ST didn't want to remove or retool it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my feeling too when I hear people blithely comment on &quot;fixing&quot; the Great Curse. Then again 2e went to great lengths to justify that mindset with stuff like Abyssals and Infernals not being subject to the Curse, Abyssal redemption freeing the new Solar from the Curse, and that comic where the ghosts of Solars murdered during the Usurpation look back and go &quot;wow, we were horrible tyrants!&quot; and charge off to be heroes again. To me the Great Curse is a parable so that the players understand what Exalted is about, but others think of it as an external mind-control forcing them to do something glorious and terrible rather than an expression of the character's personality when put under incredible emotional strain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:51:04-07:00","id":100009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99928#post99928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bit of a digression, but I sort of feel like if your game's treatment of a curse-curing plot begins with the PCs asking themselves &quot;why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; then it's indicative of a situation where the players don't really buy into the curse as a game concept but the ST didn't want to remove or retool it.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you handle it? I'd love to see a thread.<br /> <br /> And so this is not technically a derail:<br /> It means your ST can probably throw his flowcharts away now and save himself the trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T08:14:11-07:00","id":100024,"title":"","content":"To be a Solar is to be ta'veren, the corner upon which fate turns. Everyone will have an opinion of you, a goal for you, positive or negative; there can be no neutrality in your presence, no middle ground. To be a Solar is to build or destroy, create or annihilate, to gather or scatter, to be Light or Darkness, White or Black. There is no 'abide' within you, no gray zone, no subjective morality, for your power comes from your decision to change the world by the might of your innermost self and a being whose mere existence brings Virtue into undeniable contrast. Even your patience is a promise of future action.<br /> <br /> Most people, when given such a mantle to bear, take it as a Carte Blanche to do whatever they want, to define themselves as without blemish and all others as bearing uncountable sins, there for you to forgive or punish at your whims, but the core book desperately beseeches you to look deep into the heart of the raging inferno that is a human soul and ask yourself, honestly, if man could truly bear the power of angels, of gods, and not fall to utmost evil as so many bearers of light before him.<br /> <br /> I dare to hope Yes. That this time, I can wield the power of the unclouded horizon, and not burn my hands on the Silmarils that the world, by making me a Lawgiver, entrusted me to hold. That this time, the madness and corruption of power will be balanced by whatever lingering trace of a human conscience I have left after my soul explodes in unlimited majesty. I could be wrong. Pray to whomever will listen that I am not.<br /> <br /> That is what it means to be Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 03-27-2014, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T08:27:24-07:00","id":100033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brasstreader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be a Solar is to be ta'veren,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Rand Al'thor is a pretty perfect Solar character: reincarnation of ancient hero who went mad, some believe he will save the world will others believe he will damn it, wields awesome powers that are feared and hated, and the magic is corrupted with madness (though he actually knows this, unlike Solars in Exalted).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or until you ask yourself &quot;Why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; And then go on to fix the Great Cures. I've done it like... three times in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the game I play, we know a lot of Solars act strangely and go crazy. But why would we assume it's a curse?<br /> We just assume the Silver Pact's line is true: Solars have the power of perfection, and that's not a power that human minds can easily handle. Some cope, some don't (actually, one of our PCs killed himself after realising he'd killed a whole village while having a mad episode). Some cope (because some rarely limit break, or have ones that aren't really noticeable, or their limit breaks make sense for other reasons because they just have an extreme personality), some don't.<br /> And obviously Lunars are a little nuts at times too, but then they're Exalts of the Goddess of Madness, so what do you expect?<br /> But Dragonblood aren't crazy, Abyssals are crazy because Oblivion corrupts their minds, while GSPs are crazy because the Yozis corrupt their mind.<br /> No reason to suggest they're cursed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-27-2014, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T09:21:02-07:00","id":100090,"title":"","content":"A Solar does not <i>be</i>. A Solar is ever <i>becoming</i>: stronger, faster, smarter,<i> better</i> than he was the day before. His flesh is stronger than steel, his bones more enduring than the mountains, yet he can walk with the footsteps of ants and dance with the grace of wind blowing across the plains. When he sings, the gods themselves pause to take notice, and when he creates, the world struggles to be a worthy medium for his boundless imagination. And every day that passes, his genius only increases, until none can ignore his raw Excellence.<br /> <br /> A Solar is never contented with what she has. Her blade must always be sharper, and the foes she uses it against must be more worthy. Her manse must be grander, more luxurious, more potent as a source of raw Essence, and her sorcery-bound minions must grow in strength to protect that power. She needs more silver, more jade, more artifacts to add to her collection or to wield against her enemies. And if the world does not pose any more worthy challenges, she shall set out into the unknown places beyond Creation to find them.<br /> <br /> This is what it means to be a Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T09:41:02-07:00","id":100104,"title":"","content":"For me it means always having a chance. If you're a warrior you never automatically lose a fight. A twilight never automatically doesn't know something. It doesn't mean you always win, but it does mean you can always try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T10:07:27-07:00","id":100130,"title":"","content":"A Solar is that which partakes of the essence of the Sun, which is Perfection. He can't channel it all, at least not at first, but he gets better at it over time. The Perfection of the Sun is like a kind of alchemy; it is Perfecting to the dross material of the world it touches. This is most obviously seen in the Solars themselves, as they quickly grow faster, stronger, smarter, more persuasive and, in general, more competent. But it is also seen in the things the Solar touches with their Excellence: He doesn't just build objects, he creates imperishable Wonders that will last the ages! She doesn't just train armies, she trains highly drilled hosts of legendary Tiger-Warriors! They don't just rule societies, they organize models of efficient bureaucracies that operate like flawless clockwork! <br /> <br /> The Solar is also about breaking down barriers, transcending boundaries. They make mortals Heroic and Enlightened, format the chaos of the Wyld into stable, orderly lands, they reach heights of Sorcery and Martial Arts that most others never even dream existed! <br /> <br /> Like the sun in the solar system, Solars are the heart and center of Creation, around which it revolves, for good or ill. The shining center can burn, as well as warm! But without it, Creation is a much darker, colder place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T14:23:55-07:00","id":100876,"title":"","content":"To me?<br /> <br /> Creation is an ill place for such beings as us. Might makes right, and there are a whole lot of entities with a whole lot more might than we have. The only way to get ahead is to trample down your fellow human beings: tyranny, slavery, economic exploitation. The world wasn't made to be any fun for us to live it, it's just there, and ours is to eke out our short lives and avoid as much suffering as we can.<br /> <br /> When you reject that, when you fight for what you believe in rather than accepting what you can't change, you attract the attention of the Unconquered Sun. He, who was created a slave, and who led a war against His creators, did not do so merely to crown himself Ruler of the Universe: he did so out of a sense of universal justice. Those who show themselves to be both willing to fight and able to rule in wisdom, he blesses with his own Essence, so that they may reforge Creation in virtue and strength.<br /> <br /> Might makes right? No. You are a Solar. Right makes might.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T15:26:31-07:00","id":100902,"title":"","content":"Solar Exaltation is a licence to to be cool. It bestows you with the firestorm mantle of a wrathful bodhisattva. It turns you into Muhammad the Prophet and Muhammad Ali.<br /> If you use it to save the world, that's cool. If you use it to wreak terrible vengeance for imagined slights, that's cool too. If you just go sit under a waterfall for a hundred years, then yes, that's cool.<br /> That is the beginning and end of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T18:00:33-07:00","id":101009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=99795#post99795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or until you ask yourself &quot;Why do I act so strangely at times?&quot; And then go on to fix the Great Cures. I've done it like... three times in my games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This bothers me quite a bit, since it's blatantly using meta-knowledge in character. One cannot ask the question, because to them nothing is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T19:01:57-07:00","id":101024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101009#post101009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This bothers me quite a bit, since it's blatantly using meta-knowledge in character. One cannot ask the question, because to them nothing is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might realise that Solars act erratically at times, but they're mortal men who've had incredible power thrust upon them, is it any wonder they're a bit weird?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T20:06:02-07:00","id":101046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no evidence that you poop, or that you have ever pooped.<br /> <br /> That's what being a Solar is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait a minute... no poop?<br /> <br /> TIIIIIIIIITAAAAAAAAAAANS!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T21:43:37-07:00","id":101070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101009#post101009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This bothers me quite a bit, since it's blatantly using meta-knowledge in character. One cannot ask the question, because to them nothing is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am not so sure about that. After seeing a limit break a few times I suspect current Solar might catch on easier because of an increased frequency of limit Break due to harsher conditions of the lives around them creating an environment that would be perfect for identifying that something is wrong with the psyche of the Exalted. It might take years To begin to realize that a flaw exists in the Exalted. The Exigents may even help prove this as they may not date back to the primordial war, and thus they would not be effected the great curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T22:35:31-07:00","id":101097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101070#post101070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am not so sure about that. After seeing a limit break a few times I suspect current Solar might catch on easier because of an increased frequency of limit Break due to harsher conditions of the lives around them creating an environment that would be perfect for identifying that something is wrong with the psyche of the Exalted. It might take years To begin to realize that a flaw exists in the Exalted. The Exigents may even help prove this as they may not date back to the primordial war, and thus they would not be effected the great curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again meta-knowledge. In character there is no such thing as limit break, willpower doesn't have a numerical value, and limit is not cumulative, it's the gradual deterioration of a state of mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T23:03:53-07:00","id":101101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101009#post101009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This bothers me quite a bit, since it's blatantly using meta-knowledge in character. One cannot ask the question, because to them nothing is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel I should point out that the original post I made was deliberately facetious in an attempt to be humorous. Obviously I failed to communicate this properly, as it keeps getting quoted and taken too seriously.<br /> <br /> Also, it's pretty blatantly spelled out that the Great Curse is an actual curse, as in an affliction your character suffers. It's incredibly subtle and insidious, but with sufficient amount of introspection it's entirely within the realm of reason for you to realize something is influencing your decision making process beyond your own free will. (We used Perception + Integrity for self-examination, with a homebrew mechanic to determine how close we are to the truth that I wont get in to here so as not to derail the thread further)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T23:15:56-07:00","id":101104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101070#post101070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I am not so sure about that. After seeing a limit break a few times I suspect current Solar might catch on easier because of an increased frequency of limit Break due to harsher conditions of the lives around them creating an environment that would be perfect for identifying that something is wrong with the psyche of the Exalted. It might take years To begin to realize that a flaw exists in the Exalted. The Exigents may even help prove this as they may not date back to the primordial war, and thus they would not be effected the great curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing to catch on to. Real people act erratically and emotionally all the time, especially when put under incredible stress. Limit Break is just a game mechanic to represent that kind of irrational behavior that historical and mythical heroes get up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T23:25:49-07:00","id":101106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pyrosorc</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars are, metaphorically speaking, the exalts who can toss a coin and calmly tell you that it will land heads. Not because they can control the coin in midair or see its future, but from sheer will and ability to make it happen.<br /> <br /> They are the splat who look at what anyone else would consider a huge risk, accept the responsibility, and get on with making it pay off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T23:27:35-07:00","id":101108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101104#post101104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing to catch on to. Real people act erratically and emotionally all the time, especially when put under incredible stress. Limit Break is just a game mechanic to represent that kind of irrational behavior that historical and mythical heroes get up to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Real people can examine their behavior and ask what motivates them to do things. I agree with Hapless here.<br /> <br /> A character with Compassion 5 is someone who always spares the lives of his enemies and will go to great lengths to avoid doing lasting injury even to someone trying to kill him. When that same person goes into Limit Break and murders someone... yeah, he's going to ask what the heck's wrong with him. If he doesn't figure it out, he's going to keep asking.<br /> <br /> Oh, and:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=100033#post100033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some cope, some don't (actually, one of our PCs killed himself after realising he'd killed a whole village while having a mad episode).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, quality. Sounds like you've got quite a player there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-29-2014, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T00:00:50-07:00","id":101113,"title":"","content":"I think it says alot about the state 2e left the game in that almost all of the first posters in this thread posted in a position of either dislike of Solars, or not having played them...<br /> <br /> And I guess even more than 'what in Exalted resonates with you' (where I really should have posted!) this is why this dew me out of lurkerdom! AWAKEN!<br /> <br /> What is being a Solar, to me?<br /> <br /> Being a Solar is not having any excuses.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Dynasty, you do not have your culture to excuse your crimes. Unlike Heaven, you do not have your bureaucracy to excuse your murders. Unlike the Imperium you lack the religion as an excuse. Unlike Rokugan, there is no society. Unlike the Sith, there is no Dark Side. Unlike the Horde, there are no escapegoats. There is only you. Being a Solar is making a choice, and to keep making choices. From the moment you decide to play the character, to when the character is finished. You cannot give the responsibility to your realm, for as their leader, you will be their brightest; you cannot give the responsibility to your king, for of his knights, you will be the greatest. If you choose to conquer, it will be your hand coming down, and none to excuse your atrocities. If you choose to serve, you will be the face of your empire, Darth Vader or Moray Darktide, and all will know you CHOSE to follow.<br /> <br /> Being Solar is freedom and the responsibility that comes with it. Lead or follow. Run or Explore.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar is being a person, not a culture, not an order, not a religion, a person, which can belong to all of those, but in doing so, defines them as they define him. Being a Solar is being a person, not defined by his powers or world, but one that defines his powers and words by his personality, by his quirks, by his will. It is a person writ large, every quirk and hobby turned into the most dangerous magic.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar is looking at the setting books, for the first time, not as horrors to endure, but as problems to engage.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar is being human. Being a Solar is laughing and crying, it is jealously and pettyness, it is angst and anger, it is spite and hope. It is showing and indulging in the gamut of human emotion frowned for heroic PCs since forever.<br /> <br /> It is freedom and revolution, the first and last word. Being a Solar is being Exalted, and defining it for all.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar is being unlike anything and anyone else, and like every story you have ever heard.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: being a Solar is being whatever you want. *Nods sagely*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 03-29-2014, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T00:40:01-07:00","id":101122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101113#post101113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it says alot about the state 2e left the game in that almost all of the first posters in this thread posted in a position of either dislike of Solars, or not having played them...</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I think only one person said they hadn't played Solars, and no one said they disliked Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Solar is being a person, not a culture, not an order, not a religion, a person, which can belong to all of those, but in doing so, defines them as they define him. Being a Solar is being a person, not defined by his powers or world, but one that defines his powers and words by his personality, by his quirks, by his will. It is a person writ large, every quirk and hobby turned into the most dangerous magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to make another point about what being a Solar means, from an OOC perspective. And you've said something similar to what I was going to say, or at least something I can build on.<br /> <br /> Being a Solar, or rather playing a Solar, is about that character. With a Lunar, you can say &quot;I'm a Winding Path No Moon with a Salamander as my totem&quot; and you can build the character from there. With a Dragonblood, you can say &quot;I'm an Earth Aspect from House Pelleps Koizuku&quot; and build the character from there.<br /> With a Solar, you could be anyone, which means you have to be someone.<br /> What makes you cool isn't your Caste, because Caste is fairly minor, Caste is simply an expression of the character you already are (unlike, say Dragonblood aspects). What makes you cool isn't the organisation that being a Solar makes you part of, because there isn't one.<br /> This means that Solars are probably the hardest character to make as something cool, but they have the potential to be the most unique.<br /> Essentially, being a Solar does not make your character special. H/she has to already be special. Being a Solar just makes you special to the max.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:08:49-07:00","id":101130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101122#post101122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I think only one person said they hadn't played Solars, and no one said they disliked Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first reply mentions they're the ones the poster likes the least, actually!<br /> <br /> And yeah, it was just those two in the thread, but being the first reply and then another close-by, they set the tone for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T01:43:49-07:00","id":101138,"title":"","content":"Ah, I missed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:16:09-07:00","id":101206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101097#post101097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again meta-knowledge. In character there is no such thing as limit break, willpower doesn't have a numerical value, and limit is not cumulative, it's the gradual deterioration of a state of mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is, because Limit Break is a binary state of mind. Either you have Limit 0-9 and couldn't be more happy with your life, or you reached 10 and completely break down.<br /> Adding to that that Solars can only reduce their Limit by 1 per story, every single one of them is going notice that sooner or later. It's an external force, more similar to mind control than your ideals and virtues. Someone got in your head, and you don't know who or even what. Sooner or later you're going to ask questions. In a realistically played 2E game it's probably sooner.<br /> Because Solars don't look at what they did and go on with their lives. Every single Solar is going to become a transhumanist in the long run, because they are not human. Making Solar special humans and nothing more is a notion owing its existence to the Infernals. Because Internals are transhumanists, aren't they? No they're not. They leave their humanity behind for power. That's not transhumanism. What Solars do is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T05:26:59-07:00","id":101214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101108#post101108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, quality. Sounds like you've got quite a player there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bad stuff kept happening to him or around him.<br /> He had Red Rage of Compassion, and flipped out and killed some people because they were bullying a girl, I forget exactly what happened.<br /> That was the final straw, so he flew up really far into the sky (he was an Airfolk) then just dropped. And went splat.<br /> Pretty sad.<br /> You've got to respect a player who's willing to have their character kill themselves because it's realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:19:24-07:00","id":101226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101206#post101206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">realistically played 2E game</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to explain what you mean by this.<br /> Are we talking &quot;realistic&quot; in the sense that most players won't customize their limit conditions and many will pick one based on its entertainment value rather than one which accurately reflects how the character might act under extreme stress?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:23:23-07:00","id":101250,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the small number of limit conditions in the book mean it's often pretty hard to find one that fits. I find people generally pick something fitting, if they can, but often they can't.<br /> Obviously you can make your own, but it'd be nice if people didn't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:32:42-07:00","id":101254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101104#post101104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's nothing to catch on to. Real people act erratically and emotionally all the time</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! What's the point of making mehcanics specifically for this again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:34:47-07:00","id":101255,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the Compassion Virtue Flaw Red Rage of Compassion for my Zenith Caste Solar-Hero Brawler in this 2E game I play in. My character, as the high priestly smiter of darkness, would of course just mindlessly beat down the nearest cause of immediate suffering when under extreme stress. Sad that the cause of it won't last long, but it'll be fun/scary (perspective deciding that one) to watch. That said, I'd like to see more Virtue flaws catering to various character concepts, especially the more mental character types. For example, there was movie involving Batman's planned contingency plans to neutralize the rest of the Justice League should they go corrupt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2394-grifnir","name":"Grifnir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:46:31-07:00","id":101257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101254#post101254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! What's the point of making mehcanics specifically for this again?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never read the book, but my friend told me 1st ed Sidereals didn't have a limit break mechanic because they thought Sid players would probably play the characters as if they were hubristic anyway (is that true, anyone?).<br /> <br /> Sometimes I think it might be better to just tell players that Solars tend to go slightly crazy, and let them roleplay it however they feel is appropriate. I actually think the &quot;go crazy for a scene/day&quot; isn't a very good way to model the corruption and extreme behavior that the Curse comes up as in the setting fluff. But I guess that's a little awkward, as some players will go for it a lot more than others.<br /> I wondered if, essentially, Grabowski felt that power corrupts, and it should corrupt the Solars, but thought some players wouldn't agree, so put in fluff and a mechanic to force PCs to be corrupted by their power.<br /> I actually think the Curse detracts from the Solar's 1st age excesses and corruption, because it excuses them.<br /> <br /> But 90% of the time, I find limit breaks to be great fun in game, so I'm happy for them to be in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T07:56:18-07:00","id":101262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101226#post101226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have to explain what you mean by this.<br /> Are we talking &quot;realistic&quot; in the sense that most players won't customize their limit conditions and many will pick one based on its entertainment value rather than one which accurately reflects how the character might act under extreme stress?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> Suspense of disbelief is what is needed. Both for the player, but also for his character. There's a divide between things you can rationalize (&quot;It was the right thing to do&quot;, &quot;I have some deep issues that came up&quot; or &quot;Nobody's perfect&quot;) and things beyond that line. <br /> The first time having a mental breakdown and killing someone you'd never really want to kill - this can be argued with temporary insanity. The second or third time you'd probably recognize it wasn't you - there is someone else in your head. Dexter calls it the Dark Passenger. That's not that far off. At that point you've already externalized the Great Curse and Limit: It's not really you, it's something else. A derangement, a sickness of mind, maybe even possession from darker spirits. As an Exalted - especially a Solar - you can't really accept this. After all, your whole existence is about being free to choose what you do. But there is this other entitiy in you which takes that freedom away from you.<br /> <br /> In any other game the character could basically shrug his shoulders and accept that he has multiple personalities disorder. But not in Exalted and damn sure not as a Chosen of the Unconquered Sun.<br /> Not drawing that final conclussion from &quot;I have a darkness in me&quot; and &quot;every Solar goes temporarily mad sometimes&quot; to &quot;there is something wrong with Solar Exaltations&quot; is a step too far* and has to cause disbelief in the player too.<br /> <br /> A fixed/houserule version for Limit would probably circumvent this issue by making the Great Curse a permanent influence to your decisions, not only when a counter reached 10 based on things you've seen in your life.<br /> <br /> <br /> * = based on common sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:14:59-07:00","id":101271,"title":"","content":"I also think it would be appropriate for the Great Curse to be very minor at Essence 1 or 2, and get worse as you raise it, as it's supposed to get worse with elder Solars.<br /> <br /> Something that just occured to me: the most obvious explanation watching a Solar, is that they're mad. But many cultures in history thought that insanity was due to spirit possession. So checking for demonic influence would probably be one of the first things people would be looking for (but I mean dematerialised ones hanging around, not an ancient Yozi curse).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:17:00-07:00","id":101276,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh great, now I get to experience the problem of<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dirty_hands\" target=\"_blank\"> dirty hands</a> in its full glory.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101214#post101214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad stuff kept happening to him or around him.<br /> He had Red Rage of Compassion, and flipped out and killed some people because they were bullying a girl, I forget exactly what happened.<br /> That was the final straw, so he flew up really far into the sky (he was an Airfolk) then just dropped. And went splat.<br /> Pretty sad.<br /> You've got to respect a player who's willing to have their character kill themselves because it's realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, I believe he used his singing staff to cause a localised and exceedingly intense earthquake that killed almost everyone in the village. The proximate cause was hearing that someone had been ostracised and exiled for some reason; the cause of that ostracism and exile was that your character had decided not to investigate a plot hook on the grounds that it wasn't your buisiness that a couple of the locals were behaving oddly... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Suprisingly, none of this disabused the surviving villagers of the notion that it was bad luck to be in close proximity to the PCs...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T08:21:30-07:00","id":101279,"title":"","content":"I remember the singing staff, just not exactly why.<br /> As an Exalt, we have responsibilities Iozz. And sometimes that means not interfering with people's personal lives.<br /> <br /> After that, I became convinced that the locals were right about us being bad luck, what with most of them dying. That's why we beat up the hungry ghosts and then left. We were clearly no good for them (it's just occurred to me that really, we're bad luck for everyone we go near, considering that whenever we go to a city something terrible happens, whether that be plague, necromancer attacks, or whatever).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:06:39-07:00","id":101308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101214#post101214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bad stuff kept happening to him or around him.<br /> He had Red Rage of Compassion, and flipped out and killed some people because they were bullying a girl, I forget exactly what happened.<br /> That was the final straw, so he flew up really far into the sky (he was an Airfolk) then just dropped. And went splat.<br /> Pretty sad.<br /> <u>You've got to respect a player who's willing to have their character kill themselves because it's realistic.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you do. I just wanted to point that out when I saw it. I'd love to play in that group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T09:13:54-07:00","id":101318,"title":"","content":"To be a Solar is a process, a journey.<br /> <br /> A Solar is gifted with power that no human being can truly grasp. It is not only the strength to do the impossible, but the responsibility to do the impossible. But this isn't going to sink in to a brand-new Solar at first. They've lived their entire lives as human mortals in a world where they may as well be a walking sack of meat surrounding gunpowder. The idea that they can change the entire world won't even cross their mind. They'll be focused on small, personal things - what they know they can do, and might have been able to do before if they'd been just a bit stronger.<br /> <br /> Of course, before long you begin to realize that the things you thought were nearly impossible suddenly are as easy as breathing. Your strength, your intelligence, your sheer <b>power</b> begins to really sink in, and you start to shoot higher. You take on ever greater challenges, testing your abilities and pushing the limits of what you can do, all the while thinking you can make things better for yourself......and still it's easy as breathing.<br /> <br /> And as The Elegant Nova once said, you have no problems, and that <i>is</i> the problem. A solar that thinks in human terms gets everything they want from life and is going to be bored to tears before long. And as a Solar looks for any stimulation they can, they begin to think bigger. A mercenary that wanted to rule a city turns his eyes to ruling a nation. A priestess who converted a village thinks to convert the region. An assassin who killed the south's worst mortal slaver starts to plan an attack on the Mask of Winters.<br /> <br /> And only then, when you find yourself facing an actual challenge to your skills, do you realize just how powerful you are. Because <i>dozens </i>of nations bow to you now. Because a city that speaks a language you've never even heard of turns their voices to you and to the sun. Because <i>you</i> wear the Mask of Winters.<br /> <br /> To be a Solar is to think yourself weak, to realize you have earth-shattering power, and to learn to use it.<br /> <br /> To be a Solar is to learn to be great, because you can no longer think yourself as anything less.<br /> <br /> To be a Solar is to realize the crapsack world you were born into is not only fixable, but is now yours to fix.<br /> <br /> Because the cynics have had their run.<br /> <br /> Hope has returned to Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T10:51:41-07:00","id":101369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101318#post101318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Because] The cynics have had their run.<br /> <br /> Hope has returned to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is so good it should be on the back cover of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:08:09-07:00","id":101409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FromBeyond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101254#post101254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly! What's the point of making mehcanics specifically for this again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that is not how Player Characters have been played since forever. Because someone who goes sulk in his tent in the middle of a big battle is called a douchebag by the other people at the table. People on RPG.net once described the typical player character as an 'Hyperdetached Sociopath'. Exalted was clearly designed to get those people to act like... well, people, and the GC is a way to let that happen as part and parcel of the game being played, not a disruption of it.<br /> <br /> And of course it is the first thing everyone wants to excise.<br /> <br /> Alot of Exalted seems to be designed by looking at fandom, and trying to find a way to herd them into playing epic heroism. See also: why it takes a spark of Real Ultimate Power to make the mythological hero archetype playable and give mechanical support for people like Sherlock Holmes, why there are a limited, small number of Solars so the solution isn't to field armies with them as grunts, why the 'they are the authority so they will gank you if you do anything funny' Exalted type is the rarest, and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101369#post101369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is so good it should be on the back cover of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T12:29:14-07:00","id":101423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101369#post101369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is so good it should be on the back cover of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>*tilts hat* Thanks. I try.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:15:10-07:00","id":101452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101409#post101409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because that is not how Player Characters have been played since forever. Because someone who goes sulk in his tent in the middle of a big battle is called a douchebag by the other people at the table. People on RPG.net once described the typical player character as an 'Hyperdetached Sociopath'. Exalted was clearly designed to get those people to act like... well, people, and the GC is a way to let that happen as part and parcel of the game being played, not a disruption of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually prefer UCS giving you a spanking after you'd been a bad hero to 2E's Limit mechanics. Yeah, Exalted would not be the kind of game where you'd enjoy a babysitter in the sky, but it would still be better.<br /> <br /> M:tAw has higher Gnosis making reality try to get under your skin (or invert it, or turn it to acid, or bring a skineating demon from outer space to your home). At least this would scale with growing Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T14:27:20-07:00","id":101497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101108#post101108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Real people can examine their behavior and ask what motivates them to do things. I agree with Hapless here.<br /> <br /> A character with Compassion 5 is someone who always spares the lives of his enemies and will go to great lengths to avoid doing lasting injury even to someone trying to kill him. When that same person goes into Limit Break and murders someone... yeah, he's going to ask what the heck's wrong with him. If he doesn't figure it out, he's going to keep asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's concede that Limit Break is an actual in-game thing, Limit tracks were designed by Autochthon, and the Great Curse is a magical effect that makes the Exalted do things they wouldn't otherwise do and so on. I don't agree with those premises, but that is the view many take with the Curse.<br /> <br /> A character with Compassion 5 <i>and Red Rage of Compassion</i> is someone who cares deeply about all life and believes in the better natures of others. But when under the extreme stress of seeing the innocent suffer and being unable to prevent it she violates her own code and seeks justice through violence, or just destroys property to vent her frustration. And it feels cathartic to give in to urge; relinquishing partial control of the Limit Break gives you back all your Willpower points, after all. Perhaps the character feels guilt afterwards or perhaps they feel justified<i>; &quot;I did not mean to do that, but THEY just provoked me beyond reason!&quot; </i>or maybe &quot;<i>It was not right what they were doing to those peasants, perhaps the next slaver will think twice!&quot;. </i>Either way they would still own the action because people rarely conceive of themselves as lacking self-determination, which should be doubly true of powerful demigods. The position of &quot;<i>I didn't do this, SOMEONE ELSE made me do this!&quot; </i>is the realm of the conspiracy theorist and persecutory delusion, after all.<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't believe Limit is an in-setting thing. I think the Exalted are responsible for their actions and Limit Break is just a clumsy social mechanic for generating emotional and irrational behavior that resonates with the source material the game draws on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101409#post101409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because that is not how Player Characters have been played since forever. Because someone who goes sulk in his tent in the middle of a big battle is called a douchebag by the other people at the table. People on RPG.net once described the typical player character as an 'Hyperdetached Sociopath'. Exalted was clearly designed to get those people to act like... well, people, and the GC is a way to let that happen as part and parcel of the game being played, not a disruption of it.<br /> <br /> And of course it is the first thing everyone wants to excise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue the Great Curse isn't a thing one should be interacting with in-setting; the parable of the Great Curse is hidden from the actors on Creation's stage because it exists to inform us, the players/storytellers/audience, of the essential tragedy of the Age of Sorrows. Later Exalted books added material that support the &quot;alien transperfect UMI effect that makes you a jerk&quot; read of the Curse, unfortunately, so I can see why there's a visceral reaction to it from the fandom where curing it becomes a priority. A lot of the bad fluff around the Great Curse needs to be stripped out to go back to its roots.<br /> <br /> To take that tangent back to the core topic, to me the Solar Exalted are the ultimate power fantasy in a game about the nature of power. It can be your chance to be the Chosen One of your own pulp fantasy epic, but it takes place in a world where not everything is going to turn out happil<i>y </i>just because you shine gold and have a magical sword. But the Solars are passionate and virtuous and righteous so they cannot turn back from using their power. How power is used, and what legacy is left from the glorious heroics of the Solars, is up to the players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T14:47:37-07:00","id":101499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101250#post101250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the small number of limit conditions in the book mean it's often pretty hard to find one that fits. I find people generally pick something fitting, if they can, but often they can't.<br /> Obviously you can make your own, but it'd be nice if people didn't have to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people do. It's just more memorable when someone plays the pacifist healer with Red Rage of Compassion who ends up annihilating a village while screaming &quot;BLOOD AND SKULLS FOR KHORNE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T14:50:37-07:00","id":101502,"title":"","content":"Having no Great Curse and instead just people going crazy because they have power would make the setting too hopeless. The return of the Solars at the end of the Second Age might doom the world to endless cycles of rebellion and corruption, but it might actually save Creation instead. Just now someone pointed out that the return of the Solars is meant to bring hope. If the Great Curse is not external, then there is no hope for Creation to have a better future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1658-maelstromseeker","name":"maelstromseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T15:51:53-07:00","id":101553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maelstromseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101502#post101502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no Great Curse and instead just people going crazy because they have power would make the setting too hopeless. The return of the Solars at the end of the Second Age might doom the world to endless cycles of rebellion and corruption, but it might actually save Creation instead. Just now someone pointed out that the return of the Solars is meant to bring hope. If the Great Curse is not external, then there is no hope for Creation to have a better future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree in certain respects and disagree in others.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy preferred take on the setting would be that there is no Curse. You picked 300 people with no other traits in common besides that they had ambition and were willing to kill the Primordials. You are not going to get the Justice League with that criteria. Some of them are going to be assholes. Then those 300 people got given the job of ruling the entire world however they wanted, a harem of shapeshifter consorts, and advisers who are practically defined by never wanting to rock the boat. Said consorts and advisers were war buddies and thus would be even less likely to speak up if they were doing anything immoral, because people make excuses for their friends all the time. The only people who they might view as superiors went off to play the Games of Divinity and were totally willing to let them do as they pleased. This is not a recipe for an age of peace and prosperity that will last forever and ever. It is a recipe for an age that produces a lot of great works, then a lot of atrocities, and then implodes violently. Not every First Age Solar was a bad egg, but the ones that weren't were much too willing to let the ones that were get away with it.<br /> <br /> If you want to fix Creation, first, you have to come up with a better system than the Solar Deliberative was, one that doesn't give the Solars or anyone else such free reign. Then you have to win back the trust and loyalty of all the other Exalts after their bad experiences, while dealing with <i>their</i> bad eggs. Then you have to actually prove that you're not a bad egg yourself, and I hope you know how to do that when faced with choices that aren't pure black and white. It's your decision whether your character is the type of person to get drunk with power and repeat the mistakes of history, but you don't get to just say that, you have to prove it in every session with every decision you make. You can do it, but there's no Charm to help you make the right choices.<br /> <br /> If <i>that</i> was how Solars were written, I would like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/598-couch","name":"Couch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar598_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T16:31:47-07:00","id":101586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maelstromseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101502#post101502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no Great Curse and instead just people going crazy because they have power would make the setting too hopeless. The return of the Solars at the end of the Second Age might doom the world to endless cycles of rebellion and corruption, but it might actually save Creation instead. Just now someone pointed out that the return of the Solars is meant to bring hope. If the Great Curse is not external, then there is no hope for Creation to have a better future.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is to make heroes who aren't complete Mary Sues, and like most social mechanics it's primarily there to keep from all the characters becoming similarly maladjusted, as someone earlier mentioned happening with DnD's land of sociopaths. I like the idea of, but also have two major problems with, the great curse:<br /> <br /> 1) It's given an external cause but is deliberately built so the exalted can never discover it without a huge ass-pull. The closest thing to a logical reason I've ever heard to learn of the Great Curse's discovery that didn't involve rewriting part of the setting is that a Twilight caste began to notice patterns in how Exalted behaved under extreme stress - patterns that were too consistent to be coincidence. (but that is a little too meta for my taste) This makes the fall of whatever new golden age you build seem inevitable, since it's a curse specifically MADE to make you fail. It's the only thing in the entire setting that you <b>can't</b> do a single thing about. It's easier to destroy all of Creation in a single kick than to find out about the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> 2) The Flaws that it manifests in are defined within the book itself. It makes them too rigid. Virtues and virtue flaws define your character's personality - they are very personal. So why do a bunch of people who have nothing in common react to the suffering of the innocent in the same way? My Night Caste has heart of flint, but given the choice, I would have made his limit break that he utterly refused to admit defeat. (granted, I'm inexperienced with Exalted, so maybe there's more than the 2 or 3 per virtue I found)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T16:45:24-07:00","id":101597,"title":"","content":"Am I remembering incorrectly or did it say somewhere that Lytek actually knows about the Great Curse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1658-maelstromseeker","name":"maelstromseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T17:07:58-07:00","id":101607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maelstromseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101597#post101597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I remembering incorrectly or did it say somewhere that Lytek actually knows about the Great Curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>He knows there is something wrong, but doesn't act, finally showing himself as the only canon character with basic pattern recognition.<br /> And Lytek can't do much about it. Primordial level magic is a little bit too much for a basic counterspell. Autochthon is not really on anyone's speed dial anymore, and the only other ones who could remove the Curse would be Solars themselves. Now try to explain some superpowered megalomaniacs how they're actually mindcontrolled by things not even alive anymore, to be giant jerks. Telling it would not really benefit Lytek's continuing health.<br /> And then there's that small problem that basically the last 5 millennia happened while he wasn't saying anything... some people would definitely make him the bad guy responsible for the Usurpation, for the era of nightmares and what not.<br /> Yes, dear sweet Lytek probably has the worst job in all the realms of existence. He so needs an Exigent to get him out of this mess safely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T18:05:06-07:00","id":101639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kukla</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no evidence that you poop, or that you have ever pooped.<br /> <br /> That's what being a Solar is.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if you were ever to put effort into pooping, you'd poop like no man nor god has pooped before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101097#post101097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again meta-knowledge. In character there is no such thing as limit break, willpower doesn't have a numerical value, and limit is not cumulative, it's the gradual deterioration of a state of mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except people in the real world who suffer from mental deterioration sometimes notice it. People with addictions say the themselves, 'I feel like I'm losing control, something is wrong.' People with depression often overestimate that something is wrong with them. It's difficult to think of a gradual mental illness or deterioration in the real world where no one ever notices that it's happening to them or to a friend or family member.<br /> <br /> And the Exalted aren't average people. Why wouldn't a Solar doctor notice that they sometimes fly into a violent rage and they never did that before they Exalted? I mean, they could have Exalted at age 30, that's plenty of time to develop a solid sense of your 'normal' behavior.<br /> <br /> In order to explain this, the game sort of falls back on 'a wizard did it' because you just magically don't know. It's not surprising people reject that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 03-29-2014, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T18:30:27-07:00","id":101652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101206#post101206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there is, because Limit Break is a binary state of mind. Either you have Limit 0-9 and couldn't be more happy with your life, or you reached 10 and completely break down.<br /> Adding to that that Solars can only reduce their Limit by 1 per story, every single one of them is going notice that sooner or later. It's an external force, more similar to mind control than your ideals and virtues. Someone got in your head, and you don't know who or even what. Sooner or later you're going to ask questions. In a realistically played 2E game it's probably sooner.<br /> Because Solars don't look at what they did and go on with their lives. Every single Solar is going to become a transhumanist in the long run, because they are not human. Making Solar special humans and nothing more is a notion owing its existence to the Infernals. Because Internals are transhumanists, aren't they? No they're not. They leave their humanity behind for power. That's not transhumanism. What Solars do is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda feel like, if you interpret the Great Curse in light of its mechanical particulars rather than how the game describes it, you aren't really taking it seriously as a game element. Ignoring what the fluff says and attempting to extrapolate fluff from crunch alone results in making up your own game. You can do that, but it's not the game I'm talking about!<br /> <br /> Beyond that, though, I think you have an unrealistic notion of how people's minds work. Obviously we can't do this to check, but from what I've seen the evidence seems to be that even if you could inject wildly foreign thoughts into people's heads, most people would rationalize those thoughts as fitting organically into their personality and worldview so long as they were conscious of themselves while having them. The Great Curse is not foreign in that sense, because it comes from you. It is an expression of your own personality. If you have, say, Deliberate Cruelty as your Limit Break, the Great Curse is not that sometimes the curse of the Primordials makes you cruel, it is that in some respect you are naturally cruel, and sometimes the curse of the Primordials stokes that to a fever pitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":104,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","user":"Gayo","date":". 03-29-2014, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T18:30:30-07:00","id":101653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101639#post101639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you were ever to put effort into pooping, you'd poop like no man nor god has pooped before.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.weebls-stuff.com/toons/A+Walk+In+The+Woods/\" target=\"_blank\">Warning: disgustingly apropos</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T18:47:13-07:00","id":101659,"title":"","content":"You could not pay me to click that link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:18:01-07:00","id":101681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101652#post101652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda feel like, if you interpret the Great Curse in light of its mechanical particulars rather than how the game describes it, you aren't really taking it seriously as a game element. Ignoring what the fluff says and attempting to extrapolate fluff from crunch alone results in making up your own game. You can do that, but it's not the game I'm talking about!<br /> <br /> Beyond that, though, I think you have an unrealistic notion of how people's minds work. Obviously we can't do this to check, but from what I've seen the evidence seems to be that even if you could inject wildly foreign thoughts into people's heads, most people would rationalize those thoughts as fitting organically into their personality and worldview so long as they were conscious of themselves while having them. The Great Curse is not foreign in that sense, because it comes from you. It is an expression of your own personality. If you have, say, Deliberate Cruelty as your Limit Break, the Great Curse is not that sometimes the curse of the Primordials makes you cruel, it is that in some respect you are naturally cruel, and sometimes the curse of the Primordials stokes that to a fever pitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. Even if you assume that the Great Curse is an alien mental illness (it's not, or at least it shouldn't be!) people still would respond as if these urges are their own. Cruel Solar Lyta isn't going to ponder &quot;wow, I wasn't cruel 10 years ago, I must be brainwashed!!!&quot;. At best she might reflect back on all the trials she's undergone and justify to herself WHY she has become so callous. Red Rage of Compassion character likewise is going to internalize their behavior as &quot;I am someone who savagely beats oppressors to right wrongs&quot;. It will become part of their identity <i>because</i> they do these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101607#post101607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He knows there is something wrong, but doesn't act, finally showing himself as the only canon character with basic pattern recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunars, Sidereals, Dragonblooded, the Unconquered Sun and possibly large swaths of humanity all also noticed the same trends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101639#post101639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except people in the real world who suffer from mental deterioration sometimes notice it. People with addictions say the themselves, 'I feel like I'm losing control, something is wrong.' People with depression often overestimate that something is wrong with them. It's difficult to think of a gradual mental illness or deterioration in the real world where no one ever notices that it's happening to them or to a friend or family member.<br /> <br /> And the Exalted aren't average people. Why wouldn't a Solar doctor notice that they sometimes fly into a violent rage and they never did that before they Exalted? I mean, they could have Exalted at age 30, that's plenty of time to develop a solid sense of your 'normal' behavior.<br /> <br /> In order to explain this, the game sort of falls back on 'a wizard did it' because you just magically don't know. It's not surprising people reject that.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of those are external to the self. Especially addiction, it turns out. Is it possible for Red Rage Solar to realize they have an anger-management problem and seek counseling? Of course, in a white-room scenario. The Gold side of the Great Prophecy did have hope for success after all. Is it possible for them to come to that realization when they are one of an elite group of god-kings ruling over the world with few peers who can stay their hand? That's quite a different story!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:18:33-07:00","id":101683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101639#post101639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you were ever to put effort into pooping, you'd poop like no man nor god has pooped before.<br /> <br /> <br /> Except people in the real world who suffer from mental deterioration sometimes notice it. People with addictions say the themselves, 'I feel like I'm losing control, something is wrong.' People with depression often overestimate that something is wrong with them. It's difficult to think of a gradual mental illness or deterioration in the real world where no one ever notices that it's happening to them or to a friend or family member.<br /> <br /> And the Exalted aren't average people. Why wouldn't a Solar doctor notice that they sometimes fly into a violent rage and they never did that before they Exalted? I mean, they could have Exalted at age 30, that's plenty of time to develop a solid sense of your 'normal' behavior.<br /> <br /> In order to explain this, the game sort of falls back on 'a wizard did it' because you just magically don't know. It's not surprising people reject that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but these problems come from what one does to oneself, not some otherwordly death curse. The problems come from human nature and brain chemistry. Since there's likely not a thing called brain chemistry in Exalted, that leaves human nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T19:59:04-07:00","id":101702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101683#post101683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true, but these problems come from what one does to oneself, not some otherwordly death curse. The problems come from human nature and brain chemistry. Since there's likely not a thing called brain chemistry in Exalted, that leaves human nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything in our world down to the cellular level still exists in Exalted. This does leave out the more intricate parts of biochemistry, but issues like amyloid plaques would still exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:03:57-07:00","id":101704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101497#post101497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue the Great Curse isn't a thing one should be interacting with in-setting; the parable of the Great Curse is hidden from the actors on Creation's stage because it exists to inform us, the players/storytellers/audience, of the essential tragedy of the Age of Sorrows. Later Exalted books added material that support the &quot;alien transperfect UMI effect that makes you a jerk&quot; read of the Curse, unfortunately, so I can see why there's a visceral reaction to it from the fandom where curing it becomes a priority. A lot of the bad fluff around the Great Curse needs to be stripped out to go back to its roots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this 100%. I feel 3e should word the 'win condition' of Exalted not in defeating the Great Curse, but in succeeding DESPITE the Great Curse. Much like fear and hatred and all other enemies a Solar will encounter, it is to be surpassed, but it cannot be vanquished.<br /> <br /> If they word it well enough, it might change people's minds about it, as the one thing to make it all come to ruin. It should be presented with less subterfuge, as what makes it epic fantasy, and how artificial it might seem if it is removed, even though soul-surgery is how many people will still end their game; their table, their business, and it IS a valid way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maelstromseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101502#post101502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no Great Curse and instead just people going crazy because they have power would make the setting too hopeless. The return of the Solars at the end of the Second Age might doom the world to endless cycles of rebellion and corruption, but it might actually save Creation instead. Just now someone pointed out that the return of the Solars is meant to bring hope. If the Great Curse is not external, then there is no hope for Creation to have a better future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there is hope! The same hope there is for mankind. There are several theological and philsophical treatises in the real world that say there is no hope for mankind: that we will bring about our end in folly, being inherently flawed. Some believe the opposite. Exalted is a good stage to play these ideologies, and the one that has more clout on your table ought to win.<br /> <br /> There is a very good anime called Gurren Lagann; at its core it is basically a fight between Sidereals and Solars. At some point the Sidereals tell the Solars they may bring ruin to everything again, so why would they keep fighting? And the answer is basically: because we believe we won't. The choice is not to stop being human, to give up everything, but to keep going the way they are, knowing the danger they represent, and choosing not to end the world, one day at a time. That, to me, is how a good Second Age Solar should behave.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T20:49:39-07:00","id":101716,"title":"","content":"It means being at the mercy of a mechanic that allows the game to play your character for you in complete psycho mode and not being able to do anything about it. I've always preferred Infernals for their greater agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/834-hk-87","name":"HK-87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:41:15-07:00","id":101787,"title":"","content":"I want to defend the Great Curse as something people won't notice (as I said, in my group we noticed Solars are crazy, but just assume this is because they can't handle their power), but in the interests of logical debate...<br /> <br /> One point people have made is that people will often internalise things. That if you projected alien thoughts into their heads, they'd rationalise it.<br /> <br /> But...<br /> After the Tutsi massacre in Rwanda, many Hutu militia members ran away to the neighbouring countries, such as the DRC. Sociologists interviewing them about what they'd done found that a lot of people claimed to have been possessed. They couldn't accept the idea that they'd murdered and raped civilians, it didn't fit their own view of themselves, so they blamed Satan and evil spirits. They claimed (and seemed to genuinely believe) that they'd been possessed by dark forces which had influenced or forced them to do bad things, which they'd never do normally, because in their minds, they're good people. So it's not their fault, it's some external force that has made them do it.<br /> <br /> So maybe, for a Solar who has flipped out and done bad stuff, they might actually go &quot;huh, I must have been mind-controlled by someone&quot;, especially as that is something that most people know is entirely possible in Exalted.<br /> So them going &quot;I went mad and killed people, an external force from some dark power, like the Neverborn or Yozis, must have made me do it, because that's not like me,&quot; perhaps isn't that strange after all.<br /> <br /> BTW, do we want to move this discussion onto another thread? It's a fairly significant tangent from the OP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T23:59:56-07:00","id":101793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101787#post101787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BTW, do we want to move this discussion onto another thread? It's a fairly significant tangent from the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the significant tangent. We went from talking about what Solars mean us as players to discussing the Great Curse and whether or not various methods of figuring out is metagaming, or whether or not a Solar would figure it out. While that is an interesting topic in its own right, it should be discussed on a separate thread.<br /> <br /> Getting this back on topic. it appears that a common theme that is appearing is that Solars are interpreted as people with great power and can easily use that power to help or destroy Creation. I actually like this view does as it closely hews to what the developers wish to present them as, mainly larger-than-life individuals with great power but also flawed in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i147.photobucket.com/albums/r312/WuseMajor/t4q8xrt1_zps39b23a54.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/251-seifus","name":"Seifus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar251_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T08:02:17-07:00","id":101927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maelstromseeker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/99767-what-does-being-a-solar-mean-to-you?p=101597#post101597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I remembering incorrectly or did it say somewhere that Lytek actually knows about the Great Curse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was... the Maiden of Secrets (i can never remember which is which - Jupiter, i think?) knows, but is unable to tell anyone because Secrets. Lytek knows, and is trying to fix it on his own, but iirc lacks the knowledge and capacity to get rid of it. And since Lytek refuses to tell anyone, Nara-O knows as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T10:55:42-07:00","id":102033,"title":"","content":"At the OP, to me, the Solars represent the will to overcome and remake the world, to make it what you want, not what it ought to be or is, and try to make it better or grander, even if that isn't very wise.<br /> <br /> The Orichalcum Caste I see as representing the essence of what the Solars are about. They're a &quot;naive&quot;, &quot;innocent&quot;/uncynical, bright, self assured power of their own genius and excellence alone. Their essence (like the Orichalcum's resonating attributes) is one is primarily one of power, not precision or endurance. Their essence is one of <b>being unconquered</b> and they confront being conquered by their own fallibility and limits by limit breaking* and heroic madness (like Achilles in the Iliad or the Unconquered Sun under a virtue conflict). <br /> <br /> The other Exalted represent, to a degree, dealing with limits of the self through interdependence (Dragon-blooded / Jade), adaptability and fluidity (Lunars / Moonsilver), assimilating reality (Sidereals / Starmetal) and living through failure and death (Abyssals / Soulsteel), with associated vices.<br /> <br /> The Solars being strongest, I expect, is a conceit of the narrative that their essence of power and determination is nonetheless the first and foremost, despite its limits.<br /> <br /> *of course limit breaks are due to the Great Curse, but this is why the Solars' Great Curse is thematic to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}